cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "buttermilk: opinionated AI/data tools for HASS scholars"
message: "If you use buttermilk in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Nicolas
    family-names: Suzor
    email: n.suzor@qut.edu.au
    affiliation: "Queensland University of Technology, Digital Media Research Centre"
repository-code: "https://github.com/qut-dmrc/buttermilk"
url: "https://github.com/qut-dmrc/buttermilk"
abstract: >-
  Buttermilk is a Python framework that helps humanities and social
  sciences (HASS) scholars use generative AI, machine learning, and
  computational methods in a way that is understandable, traceable,
  and reproducible. It provides opinionated flows, agents, pipelines,
  and observability infrastructure for culture-first computational
  research.
keywords:
  - research
  - humanities
  - HASS
  - artificial-intelligence
  - large-language-models
  - reproducibility
  - computational-social-science
